  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td colspan="2" style="color:#655665; font-family: helvetica,arial; font-size:80%"><b>
Data on  Land&eacute; factors and  level compositions  are not available for this ion in ASD
<p/><span class="hnd">Some data for neutral and singly-charged ions are available in the <a href="/PhysRefData/Handbook/index.html" target="_new">Handbook of Basic Atomic Spectroscopic Data</a></span>
</b></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<P/>
<table style="background-color:#004400">
  <tr>
    <td colspan="2" style="color: white; text-align:center">
      &nbsp;&nbsp;Primary data source&nbsp;&nbsp;
    </td>
    <td style="color: white; text-align:center">
      Query NIST Bibliographic Database for <b>He  I</b> (new window)
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
<!--    <td style="text-align:center; background-color:#DDDDBB">-->
    <td class='brt2'>
      &nbsp;<a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for He I';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=22715&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=He&amp;spectr_charge=1&amp;type=E');return false">Drake&nbsp;2023</a>, <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for He I';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=17714&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=He&amp;spectr_charge=1&amp;type=E');return false">Kandula&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2010</a>, <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for He I';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=1368&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=He&amp;spectr_charge=1&amp;type=E');return false">Martin&nbsp;1973</a>&nbsp;
    </td>
    <td class='blf2'>
      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The energy level data refer to the isotope <sup>4</sup>He. The excitation energies of the 1s<i>nl</i> levels with <i>n</i>&nbsp;&le;&nbsp;10 were determined here by subtracting the theoretical ionization energy listed by <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for He I';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=22715&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=He&amp;spectr_charge=1&amp;type=E');return false">Drake&nbsp;2023 </a> from the experimental ionization energy of the ground level reported by <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for He I';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=17714&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=He&amp;spectr_charge=1&amp;type=E');return false">Kandula&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2010 </a>. The energies of the higher levels below the ionization limit were determined by fitting the extended Ritz quantum-defect expansion formula (Eq. 12.54 of <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for He I';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=22715&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=He&amp;spectr_charge=1&amp;type=E');return false">Drake&nbsp;2023 </a>) to the adjusted theoretical energies of the same 1s<i>nl</i> <i><sup>S</sup>L<sub>J</sub></i> series listed here as prescribed by Eqs. (12.55) through (12.57) of <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for He I';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=22715&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=He&amp;spectr_charge=1&amp;type=E');return false">Drake&nbsp;2023 </a>. Uncertainties are specified relative to the ionization limit. To find uncertainties of excitation energies, combine the given uncertainties in quadrature with the uncertainty of the ground level. The 1s2p <sup>3</sup>P&deg; levels are given with excessive number of decimal figures required to reproduce the splittings between them, which are known very precisely. The current values of these splittings are from the calculations of <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for He I';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=20736&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=He&amp;spectr_charge=1&amp;type=E');return false">Pachucki&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2017 </a>. There exist many experimental reports on these splittings. No attempt has been made here to evaluate them. The doubly-excited levels above the ionization limit require a significant update. Those given here are quoted from the old compilation of <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for He I';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=1368&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=He&amp;spectr_charge=1&amp;type=E');return false">Martin&nbsp;1973 </a>. There are 364 papers on energy levels of He&nbsp;I published between 1974 and October 2023. About half of them are devoted to core-excited levels. NIST lacks the workforce required to process such a large number of publications. The present data set was prepared by A. Kramida for the release of ASD v.5.11 in October, 2023.
    </td>
    <td class='bcn2'>
      <A HREF="javascript:void(0)" ONCLICK="popbib('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/Elevbib/make_query.cgi?spectra=He%20I&amp;method=EL&amp;method=TE&amp;method=ND&amp;method=IP&amp;method=SF&amp;method=QF&order=1');return false"
        ONMOUSEOVER="self.status='He  I: bibliography energy levels query';return true;"
        ONMOUSEOUT="self.status=''; return true;" TARGET=_blank>Literature on He  I Energy Levels</A>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
  <br>
